 Reject pending promises with an `AbortError` when `clearQueue()` is called.
 This is recommended if you await the returned promises, for example with `Promise.all`, so pending tasks do not remain unresolved after `clearQueue()`.

+#### signal
+
+Type: `AbortSignal`\
+Default: `undefined`
+
+An AbortSignal to cancel pending tasks and prevent new submissions. When the signal is aborted, all pending tasks are rejected with `signal.reason`. Already running tasks are not affected. If the signal is already aborted when the limiter is created, every submitted task is rejected immediately.
